{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Investigating ticket from sender: desktop in warehouse office not connecting to network before shift start."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0108",
  "reason": "Checking whether the warehouse office desktop assigned to the sender is online and has network or warning issues."
}

{
  "query": "desktop not connecting to network office",
  "reason": "Looking for a fix article for an office desktop that is not on the network."
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8) says his desktop in the warehouse office is not coming onto the network, and his shift starts in about an hour. Checked: account is active, not sign-in blocked, no failed logins, password set 2026-09-11, VPN access true. Triage marked user_blocked true, but the account lookup shows sign_in_blocked false, so the triage flag looks wrong. Assigned device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro, desktop) shows online: false, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:01 UTC, disk 78% free, no warnings. KB-014 (Wi-Fi connected, no internet) is written for laptops and Wi-Fi, and its quick checks did not apply since the desktop is fully offline. KB-016 and KB-024 do not match. No KB article covers a wired desktop that is offline from the network. Not yet done: confirm whether other staff in the warehouse office are also offline (possible office network or switch outage), and confirm whether the desktop is powered on and has a live network connection. Needs: on-site or remote check of BL-DT-0108 power and network port, and the office switch/network status. Time-sensitive (shift start in about 1 hour).",
  "reason": "Desktop is offline with no matching KB article and tools cannot fix it. Time-sensitive shift start; escalating for hands-on or network-level investigation."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked your account and your office desktop (BL-DT-0108). Your account is active and not blocked. The desktop is showing as offline, so it currently has no connection to the network. I've passed this to our second-level support team, marked as urgent because your shift starts soon. While you wait, please check that the desktop is powered on and that the network cable is firmly plugged in at both ends. If a colleague nearby also can't get online, please tell the team, since that would point to an office network problem. If you can't get online in time, let us know and we will look at a workaround.",
  "internal_note": "Looked up user_id 8 (James O'Connor, Operations, usual hours 06:00-14:00 Central). Account active, sign_in_blocked false, failed_login_count 0, vpn_access true, password last set 2026-09-11. Triage flagged user_blocked true, which contradicts the account data; treat the triage flag as wrong. Assigned device BL-DT-0108 is Windows 11 Pro desktop, online false, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:01 UTC, disk 78% free, no warnings. KB-014 does not fit (laptop/Wi-Fi article, device fully offline). KB-016 and KB-024 do not match. No account action taken. Escalated to Tier 2 as escalation_id 1. Tier 2 should check the office network/switch for other offline devices, the desktop's power and port, and remote reachability of BL-DT-0108. P2 with a shift start in about 1 hour.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
